 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to applications for\nlicenses; and to repeal certain provisions of such law relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S3925",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3925-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §502, rpld §502 sub 1, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3925\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to applications\nfor licenses; and to repeal certain provisions of such law relating\nthereto\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo clarify provisions of law applicable to driver's license applica-\ntions.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nChapter 487 of the Laws of 2012 amended Vehicle and Traffic Law § 502(1)\nto require the Department of Motor Vehicles (\"DMV\") to provide space on\ndriver's license applications so that applicants could request a nota-\ntion on their license that they are a veteran of the U.S. Armed Forces.\nA separate chapter (Chapter 465 of the Laws of 2012) amended the same\nsection of law to require DMV to provide space on driver's license\napplications for applicants to be able to register in the Donate Life\nRegistry.\n\nSection one of this bill would combine the amendments to VTL § 502(1)\ncontained in these two chapters into a single subdivision one.\n\nSection two repeals § 502(1) as amended by Chapter 487 of the Laws of\n2012.\n\nSection three provides the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nNot applicable.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapters 465 and 487 of the Laws of 2012 both amended the same section\nof law but, as written, could not be laid out in the text of the law as\na single subdivision. This bill is necessary to provide clarification to\nVTL § 502(1) by combining the text of these two chapters, thereby reduc-\ning confusion regarding this provision of law.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: S.8746 Referred to Rules / A.9891 Passed Assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
